{"tuid":"b2g8je1xxtqzei4u","pageVersion":15,"fetchedAt":"2026-09-30T09:55:56.751Z","record":{"colophon":{"generator":"ifdb.org/viewgame","generatorversion":1,"originated":"2025-02-22"},"identification":{"ifids":["0D966160-1B42-4CB5-9F67-85DE527ECCFE"],"format":"glulx"},"bibliographic":{"title":"Alabaster","author":"John Cater, Rob Dubbin, Eric Eve, Elizabeth Heller, Jayzee, Kazuki Mishima, Sarah Morayati, Mark Musante, Emily Short, Adam Thornton, Ziv Wities","language":"en","firstpublished":"2009-06-05","genre":"Fairy tale","description":"The Queen has told you to return with her heart in a box. Snow White has made you promise to make other arrangements. Now that you&#039;re alone in the forest, it&#039;s hard to know which of the two women to trust. The Queen is certainly a witch — but her stepdaughter may be something even more horrible... <br> <br>There are some eighteen possible endings to this fairy tale. <br> <br>Some of them are even almost happy.  <br> <br>Alabaster is the result of an experiment in open authorship. Emily Short wrote and released the introduction to the story; John Cater, Rob Dubbin, Eric Eve, Elizabeth Heller, Jayzee, Kazuki Mishima, Sarah Morayati, Mark Musante, Adam Thornton, and Ziv Wities then contributed conversation text. Afterward, the game received further editing to improve continuity and add endings, and Daniel Allington-Krzysztofiak provided illustrations."},"contacts":{"url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20090610152817/http://www.inform-fiction.org/I7Downloads/Examples/alabaster/"},"ifdb":{"tuid":"b2g8je1xxtqzei4u","pageversion":15,"link":"https://ifdb.org/viewgame?id=b2g8je1xxtqzei4u","coverart":{"url":"https://ifdb.org/coverart?id=b2g8je1xxtqzei4u&version=15"},"playTimeInMinutes":105,"primaryPlayOnlineUrl":"https://iplayif.com/?story=https%3A%2F%2Fifarchive.org%2Fif-archive%2Fgames%2Fglulx%2FAlabaster.gblorb","downloads":{"links":[{"url":"http://www.ifarchive.org/if-archive/games/glulx/Alabaster.gblorb","playOnlineUrl":"https:/